# Counting words takes two calls a turn, each of a stub: get with the map and the word, set with the map, the word and the new count. The word is loaded once.
# LOOP-LABEL: loop #
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[word]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedContiguousProperties, {{*}}:GetArrayElement)
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[found]] = Patchpoint(b@[[map]]:Register({{*}}), b@[[word]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP: Int32 b@{{*}} = AboveEqual(b@[[found]], b@{{*}}, {{*}}:CallInline)
# The count is a double between the two calls. To box it, it is converted to an integer and back and the bits are compared.
# LOOP: Double b@[[next]] = Add(b@{{*}}, {{*}}:Add)
# LOOP: Int64 b@{{*}} = BitwiseCast(b@[[next]], {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP: Int64 b@{{*}} = Patchpoint(b@[[map]]:Register({{*}}), b@[[word]]:Register({{*}}), b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP-LABEL: end of loop
# CALLS-LABEL: loop #
# A loop that calls is not cut into stretches of turns, so the loop polls on each of them.
# CALLS-COUNT-3: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-LABEL: end of loop
# The members of Map.prototype cannot be replaced, so nothing in the function reads them by name, makes their function objects or tests which functions they are.
